    ],
    "summary": "The catalog has no part called \"hex-turbo-drawer-9000\". Searching for \"turbo\" found nothing, and the only drawers are the standard classic, slide, swing, long and longbin styles plus notch and bay frames. So I built the nearest thing the configurator accepts. I swapped the full base for a north half base (piece:0,0,0;half-n), because drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. Then I fitted the standard south-half drawer on that cut face (drawer:0#0,0#cut: frame, runner, body and lid). I closed the open faces with 3 solid end caps and locked the joints. check_build passes with no issues and meshes clear. The build is 8 printed parts, about 585 g and 825 minutes to print. If \"hex-turbo-drawer-9000\" is a part you have outside this catalog, I can't model it or check its fit here.",
    "outcome": "compromise"
  },
