        {
          "name": "finish",
          "arguments": "{\"outcome\":\"compromise\",\"summary\":\"The catalog has no part called \\\"hex-turbo-drawer-9000\\\". Searching for \\\"turbo\\\" found nothing, and the only drawers are the standard classic, slide, swing, long and longbin styles plus notch and bay frames. So I built the nearest thing the configurator accepts. I swapped the full base for a north half base (piece:0,0,0;half-n), because drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. Then I fitted the standard south-half drawer on that cut face (drawer:0#0,0#cut: frame, runner, body and lid). I closed the open faces with 3 solid end caps and locked the joints. check_build passes with no issues and meshes clear. The build is 8 printed parts, about 585 g and 825 minutes to print. If \\\"hex-turbo-drawer-9000\\\" is a part you have outside this catalog, I can't model it or check its fit here.\",\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"R1\",\"requirement\":\"A hex base\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"piece:0,0,0;half-n, a north half hex base.\"},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"The base is fitted with a hex-turbo-drawer-9000 (named part)\",\"status\":\"unmet\",\"evidence\":\"No part by this name exists in the catalog or the drawer offers, so it isn't in the parts list.\"},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"The base is fitted with a drawer\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"drawer:0#0,0#cut, a standard south-half drawer on the half base's cut face. It is in the parts list as hex-drawer-body-s, frame, runner and lid.\"}]}"
